This repository holds both a piece of software and the published work of
student journalists. They are not licensed the same way, and the distinction
matters more here than the software licence does.

NOT covered by the MIT licence below — all rights reserved by their authors:

  • Articles, poems, prose, headlines, decks and bylined writing of any kind,
    including the contents of `articles.js`, `centerspread.js` and any
    `published-content.js` or `content-bundle.json`
  • Photographs, illustrations and artwork, including everything in `media/`
  • The names "The Woodley Leaves" and "Maret School", the masthead, the leaf
    device, and the paper's visual identity

Student writers and artists retain copyright in their own work. Republishing a
student's article or artwork requires that student's permission, not this
licence. If you want the platform, take the template instead:

    https://github.com/ariel-378/finalsite-newspaper-template

It is the same code with none of the journalism, MIT-licensed in full.

